    "Question #: 5": {
      "Title": "Exam DES-1D11 topic 1 question 13 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A Dell EMC SC180 is currently populated with 4 SSDs and 24 HDDs, totaling 28 disks. What is the minimum number of disks that can be licensed for expansion?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 10"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 14"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 20"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 28"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: B \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The SC180 enclosure can be connected to a SCv2080 to add additional storage beyond the base unit capacity. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The maximum number of drives that can be part of a SCv2080 as of SCOS release 7.1 is 168. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC180 enclosure contains 84 drive slots. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The minimum number of spinning (HDDs) or solid state (SSD) drives in an SC180 is 28. Drives can only be added in increments of 14. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC180 is only supported as an expansion unit with the SCv2080. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 They are not sold separately. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 If you are familiar with the SC280 enclosure, the SC180 is similar but the enclosures are not interchangeable. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC280 can be sold separately but only works with an SC4020, SC8000 or SC9000. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 It will not work on a SCv2080."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The SC180 enclosure can be connected to a SCv2080 to add additional storage beyond the base unit capacity. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The maximum number of drives that can be part of a SCv2080 as of SCOS release 7.1 is 168. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC180 enclosure contains 84 drive slots. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The minimum number of spinning (HDDs) or solid state (SSD) drives in an SC180 is 28. Drives can only be added in increments of 14. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC180 is only supported as an expansion unit with the SCv2080. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 They are not sold separately. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 If you are familiar with the SC280 enclosure, the SC180 is similar but the enclosures are not interchangeable. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 The SC280 can be sold separately but only works with an SC4020, SC8000 or SC9000. \u05d2\u20ac\u00a2 It will not work on a SCv2080."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Vote_count": []
    },
